From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: build ieee80211_duration for software rate control

ieee80211_tx_h_calculate_duration() calls ieee80211_duration() when
CONFIG_RATE_HW_CONTROL is not defined, but the function is only compiled
under CONFIG_ATBM_MAC80211_NO_USE. Building with
CONFIG_ATBM_SW_RATE_CTRL=y therefore fails with an implicit declaration
of ieee80211_duration.

Compile only the duration helper for the software rate-control path and
keep the rest of the NO_USE block (dynamic PS and friends) as it was.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 hal_apollo/mac80211/tx.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hal_apollo/mac80211/tx.c b/hal_apollo/mac80211/tx.c
--- a/hal_apollo/mac80211/tx.c
+++ b/hal_apollo/mac80211/tx.c
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 /* misc utils */
 extern int Atbm_Test_Success;
 extern struct etf_test_config etf_config;
-#ifdef CONFIG_ATBM_MAC80211_NO_USE
+#if defined(CONFIG_ATBM_MAC80211_NO_USE) || !defined(CONFIG_RATE_HW_CONTROL)
 static __le16 ieee80211_duration(struct ieee80211_tx_data *tx, int group_addr,
 				 int next_frag_len)
 {
@@ -176,6 +176,9 @@ static __le16 ieee80211_duration(struct ieee80211_tx_data *tx, int group_addr,
 
 	return cpu_to_le16(dur);
 }
+#endif
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ATBM_MAC80211_NO_USE
 static inline int is_ieee80211_device(struct ieee80211_local *local,
 				      struct net_device *dev)
 {
-- 
2.43.0
